Z||000009||mrfixit58||04-09-2001||09:59 AM||||I always like the statement, "It will be worth more if you use the stock colors". Now, come on... unless you've got some kind of ultra rare Yenco Fiero, what's color got to do with value. The only Fiero's that are bringing big (in a relative term) bucks are the ultra low mileage car that usually have good factory paint or highly modified cars with big HP motors and/or custom color paint. <P>How much did you pay for the car... $500, $1000, $2000 -- and it's got bad paint? Tell me how much a new silver paint job will add to the value (quantify in DOLLARS) of the car over a nice shiny orange or any other color. About the only thing you effect on these cars by using custom colors is the re-saleability of the car (i.e., if you chose an ugly color, fewer people will be interested in actually buying the car).<P>My advise, paint it the color YOU like. YOU will be paying for it (I assume), You will be driving it, YOU will be the one maintaining it, and YOU will (eventually) be the one selling it. But most of all, YOU will be the one ENJOYING the car.<P>Besides... I like orange,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000010||jch82||04-09-2001||10:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>"It will be worth more if you use the stock colors".<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||6
Z||000011||FieroJoe||04-09-2001||10:42 AM||||When I tell people that I am restoring my 87 Pontiac Fiero, they almost always ask "Are you going to get your money's worth out of it?"  People just dont understand that I am doing it for <I>ME</I>, because <I>I</I> love the car, it is <I>MY</I> car.  Some people just dont understand that this is just more than a car for me.  Its hard to explain with words how much I love my car and all Fieros.<P>So, if a feeling can be converted into dollars (which it never will be able to...), yes, I will be getting my moneys worth, becuase I'll get $1,000,000 worth of good feelings out of it.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||12
